where βt is the noise schedule at step t, and εt is a standard normal noise term. The hyperparameter βt determines how quickly the input becomes noisy by attenuating the input data
by a factor of p1 − βt and adding noise by a factor of √βt. For large t, where calculating the intermediate variable is timeconsuming, the forward pass can be simplified as:
zt = √αt · x + p1 − αt · ε (7)
