4.3. State-of-the-Art of FSS in MIS
The main challenges in FSS from medical imaging are accurately delineating the segmentation foreground boundaries from the background. The background is usually inhomogeneous, large, and contains tissues similar to the foreground, which exacerbates another significant challenge: class imbalance. Table 2 summarizes state-of-the-art approaches for few-shot semantic segmentation of medical imaging. In fact, FSS in medical imaging ranges from the traditional conditional approach [61], to the recent prototypical networks [62, 63, 2, 64, 65, 14] and hybrid approaches [66, 60, 67] this last exploits concepts from both conditional and prototypical networks.
